assignRoadT -- DO THE TWO = ROADS AGREE WITH A HOLDER ON THE RIGHT? (SEQ 295 R2)

The ruling (Tony, 2026-10-04): = with a holder on the right carries its group
across -- setContent sets the target's data to the argument's data -- and star
then reads through it. opAssign went back to a plain setContent in 369c121.

The SHAPE: arInner holds arSrc, arOuter holds arInner. In arDrive, *arOuter is
arInner, a HOLDER, so `arOut = *arOuter` puts a holder on the right. Interpreted,
setContent copies its group and *arOut reads arSrc's value, ARV. Jitted, the star
publishes a NODE, so the emitter routes the store through jitAssignNodeRT -- the
road that, until this stroke, refused a holder by name through assignFieldCore
("holds a group; say *") and stored nothing, leaving arOut at "none" -- and
*arOut on a field holding no group reads null.

The jitted half runs FIRST (bear-trap #25: an interpreted run consumes testing's
routing). Both reads are taken interpreted, outside the action, so they ask the
FIELD and not a jitted print.

Rows (pop.sh): AR-J and AR-I both ARV; the jit entry line present, so the jitted
half really went through jitRunAction; degrade count 0.
